title: [+ year_display +] Presidential Elections
new-page: true
view-if: rubicon_president_week == week and rubicon_president_month == month and rubicon_president_year == year
on-arrival: round = 0; marcher_candidate = "Eckhart"; collectivist_candidate = "Boycott"; unionist_candidate = "Aldermoor"; ddp_candidate = "Gesling"; lvp_candidate = "Gesling"; royalist_candidate = "Seckard"; traditionalist_candidate = "Seckard"; gold_candidate = "Gesling"; other_candidate = "Seckard"; is_unity_candidate = 0; sapd_candidate = collectivist_candidate; kvp_candidate = traditionalist_candidate; dnf_candidate = traditionalist_candidate
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/DuFour_head.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
tags: event

= [+ year_display +] Presidential Elections

An era of history is closing, and the future remains to be seen.

- @candidates: Who are the candidates so far?

@candidates
go-to: candidate_menu

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> and Chancellor [+ chancellor +] have chosen to nominate Hans Seckard—former Chief of the Commonwealth Army from 4285 to 4291, and a staunch conservative monarchist, infamous for his refusal to suppress the officers’ putsch with the remark: "Commonwealth Army do not fire on Commonwealth Army". In recent years, he was elected to parliament under the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], gradually drifting further to the radical right. He even appeared as a featured speaker at the Stowford Rally. Now returned from a military advisory mission in China, Seckard enters the race for the presidency—backed by many of DuFour’s former allies and the disgraced Staal.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, recognizing the precariousness of their position, have swallowed their pride and endorsed Seckard for the presidency. [? if not dufour_term_extended: They deem him sufficiently right-wing—after all, he once wrote to his sister urging her to vote for [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] in 4297. ?]

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> are too disorganized following Staal's crackdown, and are unable to field a candidate for president. They will be backing whoever we choose to back, provided it's a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span>.

Many <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">icans</span> of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], and <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> float the idea of running Hugo Eckhart, a nationally renowed Airship captain, as a unity candidate. While he has some nationalistic views, he is also ardently opposed to <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Imperial Sovereigntism</span>.

Barring that, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] are planning to run separate candidates in the first round if the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> runs its own candidate. The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is considering nominating Konrad Aldermoor, mayor of Calbridge and member of the Heartland state legislature. He calls for an alliance of conservative Faithful democrats that encompasses both Faithful and dissenters. The [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] might nominate Gareth Gesling, former defense minister, who has crossover appeal to conservatives in the moderate right and other parties who dislike the renewed <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span>-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> alliance.

As for the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, we could support a joint Unity Coalition candidate or run our own.

A leading candidate is Albert Grenshaw of our Revisionist faction. Former Interior Minister of Heartland and currently Axton’s Police Chief, he has played a central role in combating both <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">left</span>-wing extremism. Most notably, he helped organize the general strike that brought down Staal. However, his hardline stance against the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>—including his suppression of their demonstrations—has made him unacceptable to them.

Alternatively, we could nominate Joran Vesh, our party chairman and leader of the Centrist faction. He is palatable to the propertied parties and the <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span>, who may begrudgingly tolerate his candidacy.

@candidate_menu

- @eckener_r1: Support Hugo Eckhart as a joint Unity Coalition candidate.
- @adenauer_r1: Support Konrad Aldermoor of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].
- @gessler_r1: Support Gareth Gesling of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?].
- @grzesinski_r1: Support Albert Grenshaw.
- @wels_r1: Support Joran Vesh.

@eckener_r1
